Z||000004||88formula||12-16-2000||10:31 PM||||Never ever ever ever ever ever ever put antiseize even near the ignition system. It will reek havoc with your ignition system because it conducts electricity. It could cause the spark energy to find a different path to ground other than the spark plug electrode. Remember that stuff has metal in it. Clean the holes and threads with compressed air and install them dry.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Phaeton||12-16-2000||11:03 PM||||Putting anti-seize on the threads where it belongs will cause no problem with the ignition system.<BR>Gooping it all over the electrode or ceramic will short out the spark.<BR>Silicone grease on the ceramic will improve sealing and make the boot easier to get off again.||||reg||12
